<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maria II Zaccaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. after 1404</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maria II <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaccaria">Zaccaria</a> was a Genoese noblewoman, widow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-san-superano">Pedro de San Superano</a>, who ruled the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> from 1402 to 1404. She was succeeded by her nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/centurione-ii-zaccaria">Centurione II Zaccaria</a>, the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> prince of Achaea, who lost the remaining lands to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> in 1430.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maria-ii-zaccaria.jpg" alt="Maria II Zaccaria" width="320" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chios historian · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:House_of_Zaccaria_Coat_of_Arms.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
